\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The order of limits in the Ising model}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{A cited infinite-volume input concerns the nearest-neighbor
ferromagnetic Ising model on #{\mathbb Z^n} for #{n\ge2}, with
uniform positive coupling and inverse temperature strictly above
its critical value. On growing boxes with free boundary, take the
thermodynamic limit of the magnetization density in a fixed uniform
field #{\eta>0}, then let #{\eta} decrease to zero. The result is
strictly positive. Approaching from negative fields gives its negative.
At zero field the plus and minus boundary conditions select distinct
infinite-volume Gibbs states.
\citet{Corollary 3.7, p. 89, and Theorems 3.25 and 3.34, pp. 104, 108}{friedli2017statistical}
give the limit prescription, the coexistence criterion and the
one-sided magnetizations.}

\p{If the field tends to zero first in each finite box with free
boundary, the sign flip in \ref{fdip-00ZY} gives zero at every size.
The same finite cancellation holds with periodic boundary. In the
separate continuum quartic model, \ref{fdip-00IE} gives mixing and
uniqueness of the vacuum in its specified weak-coupling domain.}
